# Direct dependencies.
#
# Lower bounds are mandatory, not tidiness. Without them pip backtracks through
# years of releases hunting a resolution — on a cross-platform `pip download`
# it walked back to pydantic 1.7 (2020) and failed on a pyyaml pin from that
# era. Bounds keep the resolver in the present.
#
# For a reproducible bundle, compile a lockfile ON THE TARGET PLATFORM:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.lock.txt
#
# Everything here must be available as a wheel (pure-Python or manylinux).
# No PyTorch, no CUDA wheels -- Ollama owns the GPU.

fastapi>=0.115
uvicorn>=0.32
# Deliberately NOT uvicorn[standard]. The extras pull in uvloop, httptools,
# watchfiles and websockets — four more compiled wheels to vendor, for a
# throughput gain this workload will never notice, a reload feature only used
# in development, and a WebSocket transport we do not use (chat streams over
# SSE). They also break cross-platform `pip download`.
